<%# One hypothesis of the open-endedness finding: the verdict its own sweep supports, then
    the arm-by-arm counts it was read from. `reading` names the deciding observable and
    `unit` what it is measured in. %>
<p>
  <span class="badge <%= bet.badge_class %>"><%= bet.verdict_label %></span>
  <strong>
    <% if bet.verdict == :supported %>
      <%= safe_join(bet.raising_arms.map { |arm| tag.span(arm.label, class: "mono") }, ", ") %>
      reads above the control arm in most of its runs.
    <% elsif bet.verdict == :not_supported %>
      No arm of the sweep reads above the control arm in most of its runs, and every arm has
      either been measured or run to
      <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_BARREN_RUNS, "seed" %> with nothing
      emerging — the refutation condition of the hypothesis, at the seeds this sweep has.
      <% if bet.barren_arms.any? %>
        It rests on
        <%= safe_join(bet.barren_arms.map { |arm| tag.span(arm.label, class: "mono") }, ", ") %>,
        where nothing emerged at all.
      <% end %>
    <% elsif bet.control_barren? %>
      The control arm never emerged, so there is no default substrate to read the other arms
      against and the hypothesis cannot be decided here either way.
    <% else %>
      Not enough emerged seeds to decide it either way.
    <% end %>
  </strong>
  <% if bet.experiment? %>
    <%= link_to bet.experiment.name, experiment_path(bet.experiment) %> has
    <%= pluralize bet.emerged_count, "emerged run" %>, <%= bet.measured_count %> of
    them carrying <%= reading %> after the crossing.
  <% else %>
    The sweep <span class="mono"><%= bet.slug %></span> is not in this database, so it has
    no runs behind it here.
  <% end %>
  <% if bet.control_comparable? %>
    The control arm's median peak is
    <%= number_with_precision bet.control_median_peak, precision: 1, strip_insignificant_zeros: true %>
    <%= unit %>, and every other arm with at least
    <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_ARM_RUNS, "measured run" %> is counted
    against it.
  <% elsif bet.control_barren? %>
    The control arm never emerged: <%= bet.control_arm.terminal_count %> of its runs reached
    their last epoch and none of them crossed, so the default substrate has no median peak
    here and nothing can be measured against it.
  <% else %>
    The control arm carries fewer than
    <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_ARM_RUNS, "measured run" %>, so there is
    nothing to count the other arms against yet.
  <% end %>
  <% if bet.barren_arms.any? %>
    Arms that never emerged:
    <%= safe_join(bet.barren_arms.map { |arm| tag.span("#{arm.label} (0 of #{arm.terminal_count} runs)",
                                                       class: "mono") }, ", ") %>.
    <%= bet.barren_arms.one? ? "That arm holds" : "Those arms hold" %> no replicator to read,
    so nothing there stands above the control arm and the sweep counts
    <%= bet.barren_arms.one? ? "it" : "them" %> as read rather than as unseeded.
  <% end %>
  <% if bet.untestable_arms.any? %>
    Untestable here:
    <%= safe_join(bet.untestable_arms.map { |arm| tag.span(arm.label, class: "mono") }, ", ") %>
    <%= bet.untestable_arms.one? ? "carries" : "carry" %> fewer than
    <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_ARM_RUNS, "measured run" %> without
    having drawn a blank seed-block either, so the sweep cannot read as not supported until
    <%= bet.untestable_arms.one? ? "it is" : "they are" %> seeded further — an arm that has
    emerged once refutes nothing, and neither does one nobody has run.
  <% end %>
</p>
<%= render "findings/substrate_arms", bet: bet, unit: unit %>
